// Detection: a burst of connections from one source (scanning / automation)
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1046 (Network Service Discovery)
// Mirrors Wazuh rule 100110.
//
// Cowrie only exposes one port, so this is the honeypot-side signal for
// scanning. The stronger network-scan evidence lives on the attacker side
// (nmap output); this catches automated tooling hammering the SSH port.

Cowrie_CL
| where eventid_s == "cowrie.session.connect"
| summarize Connections = count() by src_ip_s, bin(TimeGenerated, 1m)
| where Connections >= 12
| order by Connections desc
